From 35a488ba889d4e77017a578063907986625a31b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: greyoak111 <151205158+greyoak111@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 23:29:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 42/48] Open the floating chat's menus over full-screen apps
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The "⋯" menu and the danmaku right-click menu are separate popup windows
and stayed out of another app's full-screen Space. Before each popup they
now join all Spaces as a full-screen auxiliary, non-activating panel. The
exclusive behaviour bits Qt sets are cleared first (AppKit throws on
conflicting combinations), and a refusal is logged instead of thrown.
The FloatingChat test hook can pop the menu up; e2e-float-fullscreen.mjs
checks it over a full-screen app.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
